as you probably know rudy giuliani has  been suspended from the practice of law  indefinitely and he may be disbarred  soon  but what's going to happen now and can  he still practice  well i was curious about that so i  looked it up a lot of people thought he  was only barred in new york that's not  actually true  rudy giuliani is also barred in the  district of columbia  side note this is important because he  filed an affidavit in one of the  election-related cases where he said  that he was a member of good standing of  the dc bar  in fact he hadn't been paying his dues  so he was not in fact in good standing  people were wondering whether that meant  that he had perjured himself in those  election cases  but the more important point is that now  that he's been suspended in new york  according to the dc bar rules he has an  affirmative obligation to notify  dc about the suspension and presumably  dc will issue a reciprocal suspension  against  giuliani so he's not going to be able to  practice in new york he's not going to  be able to practice in dc  and we're not going to see rudy giuliani  in court anytime soon
 

